{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02485",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.7,
      "end_seconds": 3.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "sorry I'm a little late, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.92,
      "end_seconds": 10.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Yes, have a a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.0,
      "end_seconds": 19.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "Well, I've been having pain at night. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.16,
      "end_seconds": 24.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "let me quickly check your readings"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.85,
      "end_seconds": 35.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.66,
      "end_seconds": 64.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "okay: respiratory rate 15, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, heart rate 64, blood pressure 126 over 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.98,
      "end_seconds": 67.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.71,
      "end_seconds": 71.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.68,
      "end_seconds": 85.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.55,
      "end_seconds": 89.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I've had it for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.36,
      "end_seconds": 98.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.09,
      "end_seconds": 116.76,
      "duration_seconds": 17.67,
      "text": "It happens on and off. I'd call it severe. There's burning pain in the upper tummy as well. About burning pain in the upper tummy, it's once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.96,
      "end_seconds": 122.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Okay, any black stools, weight loss or vomiting blood at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.23,
      "end_seconds": 127.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Uh, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.06,
      "end_seconds": 131.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.97,
      "end_seconds": 135.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Actually, I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.01,
      "end_seconds": 157.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.34,
      "end_seconds": 163.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "oh, no, I've never reacted to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.26,
      "end_seconds": 166.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.95,
      "end_seconds": 172.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "it's ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, three times a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.94,
      "end_seconds": 175.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.3,
      "end_seconds": 189.18,
      "duration_seconds": 11.88,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.13,
      "end_seconds": 195.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.98,
      "end_seconds": 200.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "let me think, my grandfather had a stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.88,
      "end_seconds": 206.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.42,
      "end_seconds": 213.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No, no conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.06,
      "end_seconds": 217.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.24,
      "end_seconds": 219.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "look straight ahead"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.97,
      "end_seconds": 235.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "your upper tummy is tender in the middle with no guarding"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.79,
      "end_seconds": 239.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.81,
      "end_seconds": 269.92,
      "duration_seconds": 16.11,
      "text": "right, here's what I'm thinking i think we're dealing with a possible stomach ulcer from anti-inflammatory tablets at this stage the reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.06,
      "end_seconds": 274.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.28,
      "end_seconds": 283.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a possible stomach ulcer from anti-inflammatory tablets do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.86,
      "end_seconds": 328.02,
      "duration_seconds": 33.16,
      "text": "Let's book a stool test for helicobacter to look into dyspepsia. A blood count is what I'd like next, for dyspepsia. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'm going to put you on omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day, eight weeks. That should help with stomach ulcer. Stop the ibuprofen and use paracetamol for the knee pain instead. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.0,
      "end_seconds": 343.54,
      "duration_seconds": 13.54,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. See me again in six weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.68,
      "end_seconds": 349.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}